# Applied Performance — Unit OKRs (2026–27)

## Vision (North Star)
**Be the best applied performance department in the country.**

That's the bar. A KR is "done" only at a level a top-5 program would recognize, not just "we did a thing."

## Mission (how we get there)
Turn Baylor's athlete data into decisions that keep athletes available and performing, build the data and performance literacy of the people who use it, and produce original research that advances both the program and the university's R1 mission.

## Structure (v3)
Three permanent **service pillars** — Data Systems & Analytics, Education, Research & Development — plus one **enabling objective** (Leadership & Visibility) that the new responsibilities document made explicit: the unit now delivers through people and processes Eric directs, not only through work Eric performs. Role-language definitions (Oversee, Assist, Support-and-guide, Unified) live in [[Applied-Performance-JD-2026/CONTEXT]].

**Cycle mechanics:** KRs are committed per semester (quarterly rhythm retired 2026-07-17 — decision 0007). Every KR is scored at the mid-semester checkpoint (on-track/off-track) and at cycle close (0.0–1.0, keep/retire/add). The biweekly Friday report to Chris is the standing pulse between checkpoints. Every KR must have its critical path inside the unit's control — no KR whose completion depends on an external party's timeline.

**Eric's protected hands-on lanes** (not delegated, not reviewed-only — built by his hands): HPI protocol and its dashboarding; technology vetting; white-paper analysis; one-off report and dashboard creation for sports. Delegation stops at these boundaries.

---

## Objective 1 — Data Systems & Infrastructure
> **The data layer is standardized, governed, and survives staff transition; sport-facing delivery is bespoke on top of it and routinely drives coaching decisions.**

*"Unified" means standardized underneath (metric definitions, data model, freshness), bespoke on top (per-sport dashboards and reports). A single all-programs dashboard is explicitly not the goal (decision 0008).*

**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**
| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1.1 | **Per-sport coach dashboards in routine weekly use** — Football (delivered through AJ) + Volleyball (direct) — built on shared data standards. *"Used" = referenced in the team's weekly planning meeting; core metrics fresh same-day.* | AJ (FB), Eric (VB) | ≥5 of 6 weeks, Jul 15 – Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 1.2 | **Technology decision matrix revived and adopted as standard vendor intake** — documented + Chris sign-off in writing. No named vendor; the next real pitch flows through it. | Eric | Adopted by Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 1.3 | **HPI protocol v1 drafted** — data integration, flow, storage, dashboarding, interpretation — circulated to Chris + Kenny for feedback; walked through with Kenny in a meeting Eric schedules. | Eric | Circulated by Aug 31 | ⬜ |

**Staged to Fall:** data-continuity plan per NCAA Best Practices document (what survives a staff transition — informed by the Blake departure); website-era distribution architecture; Kitman/data-management system improvements.

## Objective 2 — Education
> **Applied Performance is a recognized source of education in the building — a launched, running engine, not an aspirational one.**

*Reset 2026-07-17 (decision 0006): the original 6-issue target was 0-for-3 at mid-July. The blocker was launch — an open-ended sign-off loop and distribution re-planning around the unlaunched website. New rules: advance-notice, not approval-seeking ("shipping on X unless you want changes"); email distribution now, website as the Fall upgrade.*

**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**
| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2.1 | **Engine launched — 2 issues shipped**: Issue #1 ~Aug 1 anchored by the sleep education module; Issue #2 ~Aug 22 anchored by the GLP-1/performance brief. Proof-of-concept to Chris + stakeholders the week before Issue #1 with a stated ship date. | Eric | 2 issues by Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 2.2 | **Both leadership-requested modules circulated** — sleep education + GLP-1 brief in named stakeholders' hands for feedback (the initiative signal the Jul 9 meeting asked for). | Eric | Circulated by Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 2.3 | **Reach + demand baseline** — distribution counts recorded at each issue; inbound requests tracked. Targets set from evidence at the Aug 31 review, not guessed now. | Eric | Baseline recorded | ⬜ |

**Staged to Fall:** cadence set from evidence (monthly floor); website distribution; staff/athlete live-session targets; AP Clinic contributions as directed by Courteney (she owns the event — Eric assists).

## Objective 3 — Research & Development
> **A real R&D engine — committee, repository, formalized partners — that produces publishable output and visibly feeds Baylor's R1 strategy.**

**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**
| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 3.1 | **BAIR Steering Committee organized** — vetting process documented, first meeting scheduled with agenda. | Eric | By Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 3.2 | **Research repository MVP live** — catalog of projects, status, data, partners. | Eric | By Jul 31 (score honestly at review if late) | ⬜ |
| 3.3 | **≥1 academic partnership formalized** — named project, written scope + timeline. | Eric | By Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 3.4 | **White paper drafted** — converted from the existing short report. Eric sole owner of the critical path; Blake credited as co-author, zero dependency on post-departure contributions (decision 0005). Publication deployment = Fall. | Eric | Drafted by Aug 31 | ⬜ |

## Objective 4 — Leadership & Visibility (enabling)
> **The director model demonstrably works: staff own their lanes, leadership is never surprised, and the department's work is visible without being asked for.**

**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**
| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 4.1 | **Friday report cadence live** — biweekly email to Chris: Shipped / In Progress / Decisions Needed / Risks–No-Surprises / Next Two Weeks, <300 words. The decision-impact log feeds "Shipped" (it is no longer a standalone KR — it's ammunition). | Eric | ≥3 sent by Aug 31 | ⬜ |
| 4.2 | **AJ full handoff through fall camp** — AJ owns camp planning and the plan-vs-actual review to the football staff (framework already jointly presented); Eric reviews all artifacts pre-delivery, weekly 1:1 standing (decision 0004). | AJ, Eric oversight | 100% of camp practices on framework; review delivered ≤1 wk post-camp | ⬜ |
| 4.3 | **Noah mentoring cadence** — onboarding checklist written; weekly 1:1; departmental policies/procedures walked through. | Eric | Checklist + cadence live by Aug 15 | ⬜ |
| 4.4 | **Proactive supervisor meetings held** — Kenny (HPI/research walkthrough) + H&W technology guidance, both initiated by Eric. | Eric | Both held by Aug 31 | ⬜ |

---

## Aug 31 review (cycle close)
Score each KR 0.0–1.0, keep/retire/add, then author the **Fall (Sep–Dec) set** — first semester cycle, mid-semester checkpoint ~Oct 15. Set education reach targets and newsletter cadence from actuals. Fall candidates already staged: continuity plan, white-paper publication, website distribution, Linda's role integration (pending the Chris conversation), data-management system build.

## Parking lot
- White paper **published** — Fall.
- Peer-reviewed submission — the longer-horizon outcome behind the white papers.
- Year-end research summary — Spring close.
- Website-based education hub (with Cody) — Fall distribution upgrade.

## Superseded (v2 → v3, 2026-07-17)
- ~~Unified single dashboard across programs~~ → per-sport on shared data standards (0008).
- ~~6 newsletter issues / twice-monthly~~ → launch-first reset, 2 module-anchored issues (0006).
- ~~Quarterly KR cycles~~ → semester cycles + mid-semester checkpoints (0007).
- ~~Eric delivers fall-camp framework + Aranda review~~ → AJ owns, Eric oversees (0004).
- ~~Decision-impact log as KR 1.3~~ → fuel for the Friday report (not scored separately).
- ~~Blake as unit member / KR co-owner~~ → departed; ownership redistributed (0003).
